%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b3f2a8c8f344355b16a4d4296ae3f98, type: 3}
  m_Name: Stoat
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  vesselClass: 15
  entries:
  - Element: 3
    AbilityLabel: Field Dipole
    AbilityDescription: 'MASS MODE triggers. Squeeze a trigger and a sink-source pair (a black hole and a
      white hole, joined as a wormhole) is laid 250 u ahead, the poles together, in the
      frame you had then. The triggers'' DIFFERENCE pulls the poles apart sideways - the
      sink on the deeper trigger''s side - and their SUM pulls them apart lengthways, the
      sink always the nearer. Let go and the pair slams together and annihilates (throwing
      the Charge ripple); every press lays a fresh pair. The field bends your flight and
      anything that crosses the sink''s horizon goes through it: you come out of the
      source; a rival vessel comes out stripped of its crystals, left on the sink''s side;
      a creature is swallowed (killed); a prism vanishes. Space is the pair''s reach - one
      dial, read live: both poles'' horizon and pull x1 -> x2 at level 10
      (StoatDipoleConfigSO.poleSize), and in Time mode the orbit''s radius x1 -> x1.4
      (StoatSlingConfigSO.orbitReach). R_VesselActions/STOAT_DIPOLE.md.'
    Input: 2
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Accretion
    UpgradeDescription: 'What the sink swallows is YOURS. Prisms it takes are STOLEN instead of destroyed -
      they come out of the source in your domain (Prism.Steal, a super-steal: a shield is
      no answer to a horizon) - and every one swallowed GROWS both poles, +4% each up to
      twice their size, until the pair annihilates (StoatDipoleConfigSO.accretionPerPrism
      / accretionMax). Gated on IsUpgradeActive(Space), replicated: every peer steals the
      same prisms, and the grown size reaches peers as the published horizon. (Theft, the
      earlier Space 5, is fused in - one element, one level-5.)'
  - Element: 4
    AbilityLabel: Pathfinder / Time Mode
    AbilityDescription: 'Passive. The path your hull will fly on the inputs you hold right now, run 1200 u
      ahead through your dipole''s field and drawn as dots from the nose (blue-grey). When
      your poles WARP that path at all - it bends 3 degrees or more, or it goes through
      the wormhole - it turns lime and you fly down it faster: a warp of the hull''s own
      flight clock. TIME MODE (B): the triggers lay an attractor beside you and the hull
      ORBITS it; release a quarter-turn round (90 deg +- 15) for the whole slingshot kick,
      a fifth of it outside the window - the line becomes the rest of the orbit and turns
      lime inside the window. Time is rate - one dial, the Stoat''s boost: the warp x2.5
      at rest -> x5 at level 10 (StoatDipoleConfigSO.boost), and the slingshot''s kick by
      the same ratio (BoostRatio, x1 -> x2).'
    Input: 0
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Foresight
    UpgradeDescription: 'The pathfinder also draws the predicted paths of the three nearest rivals within
      1500 u, in their domain colours - each flown 500 u forward on the turn and speed it
      is holding right now, measured from its pose (no input needed). Read a rival''s line
      and lay your sink across it. Gated on IsUpgradeActive(Time), replicated; drawn for
      the local pilot only (StoatPathfinderExecutor.Foresight).'
  - Element: 1
    AbilityLabel: Ripple
    AbilityDescription: 'Passive, anti-vessel and anti-creature. Every pair of yours that annihilates - a
      dipole let go, an orbit''s pair closing after its slingshot - throws a SPACE-TIME
      RIPPLE from where the poles met: a spherical wave that bends the scene as it passes.
      Where its front sweeps over them, rival vessels are STRIPPED of one whole petal of
      every element they hold (shed as crystals around them; a ward against blasts stops
      it) and creatures are killed. It touches no prism, and never you or a teammate. The
      ripple''s reach is the separation the poles had when you let go (x0.6, 30 -> 160 u)
      - Charge scales it x1 -> x2 at level 10 (StoatRippleConfigSO.reach, replicated
      level).'
    Input: 0
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Siphon
    UpgradeDescription: 'The petals the ripple strips come straight to YOU instead of being shed as crystals
      - a rival''s level becomes yours. Gated on IsUpgradeActive(Charge), replicated, so
      every peer moves the same petals (StoatRippleConfigSO.siphonOnChargeUpgrade).'
  - Element: 2
    AbilityLabel: Mass / Time Mode
    AbilityDescription: 'B (on a phone, this card) steps the Stoat through its three modes, Mass -> Time ->
      Gate -> Mass, and a switch lets go of whatever the triggers held; the card''s icon
      shows the mode. MASS MODE (the default): the triggers lay the Field Dipole and the
      trail is laid THICK - the prism''s height x3 at Mass 0 -> x6 at level 10
      (StoatModeActionSO.massModeThickness, read at the replicated level so every peer
      lays the same trail). TIME MODE: the triggers fly the orbit slingshot (see Time) and
      the trail is laid at its own thickness. GATE MODE: a warp gate. Squeeze a trigger
      and a black hole opens ahead of your nose, its white hole further along the same
      line; squeeze deeper to stretch it. Fly into the black hole and you come out of the
      white hole warped - most for a long gate entered straight down its line. Let go and
      it falls together in under a second. One gate at a time.'
    Input: 7
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Armoured Wake
    UpgradeDescription: 'Every prism laid in MASS MODE arrives SHIELDED. Gated on IsUpgradeActive(Mass),
      replicated, per lay - so every peer lays the same tier
      (StoatModeActionSO.massUpgradeShieldsInMassMode).'
